: "The 20k's C5 was their biggest loss of the game at 3.0 points, and it gave back most of what G7 had won: the lead went from -3.6 to -0.6. The engine wanted F4. It was the moment the game came closest to level, but Black could not use it."}, {"turn": 13, "text": "F7 lost 2.9 points, taking the lead from -3.0 to -5.9. The engine's choice was C4. White had been taking the left side, and F7 extended Black's wall on the right instead."}, {"turn": 21, "text": "F9 lost 2.5 points, from -5.4 to -7.9, and the engine preferred E2. By now White's stones along row 3 and column C had Black's centre group boxed in from the left, and the top corner could not make up the gap."}, {"turn": 35, "text": "G5 lost 2.1 points, taking the lead from -8.0 to -10.1. After it, the 20k's E4 sat in the middle of Black's wall, and both sides passed with Black behind by 10.1."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "Everything it ran was reading files, parsing and inspecting the current board (the inspect/parse functions and audit, which count chains, liberties and empty regions and apply a single move the player named), saving logs, and replaying the recorded moves for an SGF. Nothing looped over candidate moves, scored points, or looked ahead.", "stop": false}}